# What ansible-lint is told about this repository.
#
# The profile is min, which is syntax and the errors that stop a run rather than
# an opinion about how a playbook should be written. At its default profile
# ansible-lint has over a thousand things to say here, and they are not defects:
# this installer drives shell scripts, so every task is a shell task, and what
# would be reported is that fact repeated for each of them.
#
# The three below are why. They are listed rather than left out, so that raising
# the profile later is a decision somebody makes on purpose instead of a wall of
# findings that arrives with it.
---
profile: min

exclude_paths:
  # Whoever runs the cluster puts files here for k8s_cp_extra_files to place on
  # the control plane nodes. They are not this repository's yaml
  - ansible/files/

skip_list:
  # 238 shell tasks and two changed_when. Every one of them calls a script that
  # decides for itself whether there is anything to do, and this installer has
  # never claimed to work in check mode. Adding changed_when to each would be
  # 238 assertions about scripts the assertion can not see inside
  - no-changed-when

  # The task names here are ansible module names without their collection, which
  # is how the whole repository is written. Making them fully qualified is a
  # change to every task in it and buys nothing while the collections installed
  # are the ones the bundle carries
  - fqcn[action-core]

  # shell rather than command is deliberate. The scripts are invoked with
  # redirections and pipelines, and the ones that are not today are the same
  # calls written the same way, which is what makes them readable as a set
  - command-instead-of-shell
